WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.170 --> 00:00:05.200
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and welcome to
anime club reboot edition.

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:09.580
Today will be all about the best anime reboots
and sequels in honor of the fairy tale, fate/stay,

00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:13.790
Pokemon, Jojo’s Bizzare Adventures, black
butler and sailor moon all coming back.

00:00:13.790 --> 00:00:17.280
First things first, congratulations to the
winners from last week’s miyazaki edition.

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:20.520
Melaknee, you won the Studio Ghibli DVD and
Izzy Goggin, you get to choose any series

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:21.910
you want for a future anime club video.

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:23.400
I’ll be messaging you both for details.

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:26.210
I’ll be randomly selecting one subscriber
from the comments to receive a figure of their

00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:28.279
choice from the crunchyroll store (twenty
five dollar max).

00:00:28.279 --> 00:00:31.289
and one random subscriber to pick a topic
for a future anime club video.

00:00:31.289 --> 00:00:34.210
So let’s start with our top 5 anime reboots
and sequels If you want to add any just make

00:00:34.210 --> 00:00:35.210
sure to say why you thought it was awesome
or terrible.

00:00:35.210 --> 00:00:36.210
Number 5 - Evangelion.

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:39.269
The tv series original ending was so confusing
that the first film was made to provide some

00:00:39.269 --> 00:00:40.269
clarity.

00:00:40.269 --> 00:00:42.970
It wasn’t really until the second film that
I was blown away.

00:00:42.970 --> 00:00:45.199
That film is really the reason I put this
on my list.

00:00:45.199 --> 00:00:48.920
That being said most of the reviews of the
third film make it sound like it goes overboard

00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:51.010
on the visuals and is kind of hard to follow.

00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:52.600
Like one giant boss fight.

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:54.640
There is a fourth movie being made for 2015.

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:56.379
So hopefully that will address some of the
criticisms.

00:00:56.379 --> 00:00:59.600
You can’t just spend all of your time in
a boss fight.

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:01.020
Character development is important.

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:04.540
4 Jojo’s Bizzare adventures.

00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:07.540
The OVA series from 2000 still holds up today.

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:10.890
Originally there were two OVA stories but
they told a single story.

00:01:10.890 --> 00:01:15.710
The funny thing is that the newer series told
the first half of the story.

00:01:15.710 --> 00:01:19.740
So there’s this weird effect where the animation
quality drops dramatically as you reach the

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:21.420
second half of the story.

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:23.649
Both have this really classic hand drawn 90s
style to the animation.

00:01:23.649 --> 00:01:26.630
My favorite aspect of the story were the stand,
their spirit companions.

00:01:26.630 --> 00:01:27.630
they could take different forms.

00:01:27.630 --> 00:01:29.009
Not just humanoid, but also objects and elements.

00:01:29.009 --> 00:01:35.159
3 Ghost in the shell stand alone complex - I’m
talking about the laughing man arc.

00:01:35.159 --> 00:01:39.240
I was a huge fan of the film and the laughing
man episodes really embodied all of the best

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:40.240
aspects of the original.

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:45.829
The character designs were changed to resemble
the manga and because it didn’t have the

00:01:45.829 --> 00:01:49.520
time constraints of a movie, the character
development was so much better.

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:55.200
The only real complaint I had about it was
the confusing plotting of the laughing man

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:57.109
episodes and the one-off episodes.

00:01:57.109 --> 00:02:00.979
2 - Hunter X Hunter 2011 - There are so many
things to love about this.

00:02:00.979 --> 00:02:03.680
The character development is great.

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:06.990
It actually follows a classic shounen style
where you see Gon evolve over time.

00:02:06.990 --> 00:02:09.770
And it’s not just jumping from one battle
to the next.

00:02:09.770 --> 00:02:11.630
But the battles are amazing.

00:02:11.630 --> 00:02:15.349
They’re plotted out in this really strategic
way that reminds me of some of my favorite

00:02:15.349 --> 00:02:16.650
rpg games.

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:20.480
This is a really good anime to watch if you
like a story that’s easy to follow but has

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:22.950
amazing characters and a great soundtrack.

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:25.849
I listen to the character’s themes sometimes
when I’m playing games.

00:02:25.849 --> 00:02:31.370
1 - Fullmetal Alchemist Brotherhood - In my
opinion, the best anime remake of all time.

00:02:31.370 --> 00:02:35.680
A lot of the fandom considers brotherhood
to be a much truer adaptation of the manga.

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:40.049
It also introduces new characters throughout
it’s run which is pretty rare for anime

00:02:40.049 --> 00:02:41.049
series.

00:02:41.049 --> 00:02:45.491
If you have a friend that wants to get into
anime, this would be the series you would

00:02:45.491 --> 00:02:46.610
want to show them first.

00:02:46.610 --> 00:02:48.120
And it’s all on netflix.

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:51.769
Even though there are a ton of characters
by the end, all of them are well developed

00:02:51.769 --> 00:02:55.670
and three dimensional, even the villains have
hearts and clear intentions.

00:02:55.670 --> 00:02:59.900
And as an added bonus, the dubbed versions
are good.

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:03.750
Most of the time I would say stick to subs,
just because original voice casts tend to

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:04.750
be better.

00:03:04.750 --> 00:03:06.650
But in the case of brotherhood the dubs really
hold up.

00:03:06.650 --> 00:03:10.409
The only real criticism I have of it is that
the animation on the early episodes isn’t

00:03:10.409 --> 00:03:12.360
quite as spectacular as the original.

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:15.400
I think they were probably just trying to
save money for later episodes.

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:19.459
Everything still looks great, but the early
animation is just a weak point.

00:03:19.459 --> 00:03:24.150
Now it’s your turn to let me know what your
favorite anime remake or sequel is.

00:03:24.150 --> 00:03:25.329
And bonus question.

